+# Add t and check PlaceBlock arguments with it
+
+## Summary
+
+- Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker as a dependency in
+  `pesde.toml`, installed from Wally through pesde like the other packages:
+  `t = { wally = "osyrisrblx/t", version = "=3.1.1" }` (3.1.1 is the newest version on the Wally
+  index). It installs into `roblox_packages`, so it appears as `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t` and
+  both server and client remotes can use it.
+- `BlockPlacement.server.luau` now checks the PlaceBlock arguments with
+  `t.tuple(t.string, isVector3WithoutNan)` in place of the hand-written `typeof` checks.
+- Adds t to the package table in `README.md`.
+
+## Checks kept in the PlaceBlock handler
+
+| Check | Before | After |
+|---|---|---|
+| Block type name is a string | `typeof(blockTypeName) ~= "string"` | `t.string` in the tuple |
+| Position is a Vector3 | `typeof(position) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3`, inside `isVector3WithoutNan` |
+| Position has no NaN component | `position ~= position` | Same comparison, inside `isVector3WithoutNan`. t has no NaN check for Vector3 |
+| Block type exists | `BlockTypes.ByName[...]` lookup | Unchanged |
+| Rate limit, character and root part, cell above ground and free, reach | | Unchanged |
+
+Handler arguments stay typed `unknown`. t has no Luau types, so after the check passes, the
+handler casts them to `string` and `Vector3`.
+
+## Before testing
+
+1. **Stop `rojo serve`** if it is running, then **run `pesde install`** at the repo root. Until
+   you do, `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t` doesn't exist, and `BlockPlacement` errors on its
+   `require` the moment the server starts. Restart `rojo serve` afterward and reconnect the Rojo
+   plugin.
+2. **Commit the updated `pesde.lock`** that the install writes. This PR changes `pesde.toml`
+   only, because the install couldn't be run when the change was written. CI and other
+   checkouts need the lock entry.
+3. Regenerate the sourcemap (`rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json
+   --include-non-scripts`) before running `luau-lsp analyze`, so it can resolve the new package.
+
+## Testing
+
+Already run: `stylua --check` and `selene` pass on the changed script. `luau-lsp analyze` and a
+playtest have not been run yet, because they need the package installed.
+
+After installing, in a playtest:
+
+- [ ] Placing a block from the client still works.
+- [ ] From the client command bar, each of these places nothing and logs no server error:
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer(123, Vector3.new(0, 4, 0))` (name is not a string)
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("<valid type>", "x")` (position is not a Vector3)
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("<valid type>", Vector3.new(0/0, 4, 0))` (NaN)
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("NotAType", Vector3.new(0, 4, 0))` (unknown type)
+- [ ] `luau-lsp analyze` (the command in the README) reports nothing new.
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
